    "text": "The figure shows a system of two concentric spheres of radii <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> and kept at temperatures <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math>, respectively. The radial rate of flow of heat in a substance between the two concentric spheres is proportional to<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/content_2729.png\" style=\"line-height: 1.6em; width: 234px; height: 216px;\" />",
